      "hints": [
        "Expand \\(R\\cos(\\theta-\\alpha)=R\\cos\\theta\\cos\\alpha+R\\sin\\theta\\sin\\alpha\\) and match coefficients.",
        "Thus use \\(R\\cos\\alpha=\\sqrt6\\) and \\(R\\sin\\alpha=3\\); squaring and adding gives the exact positive \\(R\\).",
        "Divide the coefficient equations to obtain \\(\\tan\\alpha=3/\\sqrt6\\), then evaluate \\(\\alpha\\) in degrees to 2 decimal places."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "State $R=\\sqrt{15}$",
        "Use trigonometric formulae to find $\\alpha$",
        "Obtain $\\alpha=50.77^\\circ$",
        "$R=\\sqrt{15}$ and $\\alpha=50.77^\\circ$, so $\\sqrt6\\cos\\theta+3\\sin\\theta=\\sqrt{15}\\cos(\\theta-50.77^\\circ)$."
      ],
